title: Payers › Rules › Read the rules
route: /payers/summit?tab=rules
intro: Four rules for one payer, each closed on its first line. A rule opens to a few plain lines with the agents that use it and the date it was last saved in Psyflo. The saved lines are what New case reads for this payer; editing them is the next diagram. The rules are demo data: none is shown as verified by the payer. In the product, each field would carry a source and a confidence (published, payer-confirmed, observed, staff-reported, unconfirmed).
dir: TD
---
start s1 "Click the 'Rules' tab"
screen tab "Rules tab\nBanner if edits wait, then one card 'Rules the agents follow'\nwith an info icon and four closed rules"
decision dU "Edits saved but not yet\napplied to open drafts?"
toast bU "'1 edit applies to new drafts only'\nwith 'Update 2 drafts'\nSent requests keep what they were sent with"
goto gU "Continues in: Payers › Edits waiting › Update drafts"
click tip "Hover, focus or click the info icon\n(button 'About these rules')"
overlay tipt "'Open a rule to read it or edit it. New drafts use a saved edit at once.\nSent requests keep what they were sent with. Click Update drafts to redraft open ones.\nThese are demo rules, not verified against Summit's current policy.'"

group gC "Four closed rules, each a button with aria-expanded"
  screen c1 "Submission windows\n'Notice within 24 hours of admission, and 2 more'  3 lines\nNotice differs by payer (72 hours for Harborview, by phone for Evergreen, by fax for Lakeshore)"
  screen c2 "Backdating\n'Summit does not backdate an authorization, and 2 more'  3 lines\nBeacon backdates within 2 business days, Evergreen up to 3 days with a call log,\nLakeshore to the fax receipt date"
  screen c3 "No authorization needed\n'Individual therapy, and 3 more'  4 lines\nShown with green ticks once open (Evergreen has no crisis line)"
  screen c4 "Peer-to-peer and appeals\n'Peer-to-peer call within 3 business days of a denial, and 3 more'  4 lines\nCardinal 2 days. Evergreen ends in a state hearing"
endgroup

click op "Click a rule (or Enter, Space)"
process opn "Rule opens: its lines, then the foot line\nClick again to close"
process ub "Foot line\n'Used by Cadence and Scrubber · saved 10/12'"
process who "Used by\nWindows: Cadence, Navigator\nBackdating: Cadence, Scrubber\nNo authorization needed: Verify, Criteria\nPeer-to-peer and appeals: Advocate, Cadence"
process cf "'Saved' is the date the rule was last saved in Psyflo\nEvergreen shows 10/09, the others 10/12\nIt moves to today when a rule is edited\nIt is never a date the payer confirmed anything"
process src "A rule edited here adds\n'Source: Edited in Psyflo by {viewer}' (the person viewing when it was saved; Jordan Perez at the start)\nA rule that was not edited shows no source of its own:\nthe header says 'Source: Demo sample rules, version 2026.3'"
process noeff "New case reads the saved lines for the payer\nand level of care of each draft\nSee the New case diagrams for what it checks"
click ce "Click 'Edit' inside an open rule\n(the button is named 'Edit Backdating' and so on)"
goto gE "Continues in: Payers › Rules › Edit a rule"
goto gF "Continues in: Payers › Configuration feeds the rest of the app"
goto gP "Continues in: Payers › Header › Policy status and the demo-rules label"

s1 --> tab --> dU
dU -->|Yes| bU --> gU
dU -->|No| c1
bU --> c1
tab -.-> tip --> tipt
c1 --> c2 --> c3 --> c4
c1 --> op --> opn --> ub --> who --> cf --> src
src --> ce --> gE
c4 -.-> noeff
noeff -.-> gF
src -.-> gP
